    <p class="eyebrow">About Gautam</p>
    <h1>How it started</h1>
    <p>In 2015 Gautam weighed 115 kg and couldn't climb a flight of stairs without stopping. He took up CrossFit to lose weight and get back to the fitness he had in school. Around the same time, a bike store opened below the CrossFit studio, and that's how he found endurance sport. His first timed 10K was in November 2015.</p>
    <p>Since then he has raced 10Ks, half marathons and marathons, at least four trail 50Ks and the Comrades Marathon, and started a 100K mountain ultra in Hong Kong. He's a Super Randonneur and has done multi-day bike tours. More recently he has added triathlon, including Ironman 70.3 Goa, and Hyrox to his own racing, and both are now part of what he coaches.</p>
    <p>Gautam started coaching runners in October 2019 with three athletes. A chartered accountant by qualification, he spent nine years in tax consulting before becoming a full-time coach in 2022. He also co-hosted The Indian Cycling Podcast's coverage of the 2026 Tour de France.</p>
    <p>His coaching starts with understanding each athlete's goals and motivations, then building a plan that balances training with work and life.</p>
  </div>
